Description
Our Client, National Housing Corporation (NHC) is a statutory body established by an Act of Parliament Cap. 117 whose mandate is to implement the Government’s Housing Policies and Programmes. NHC is seeking to recruit results-driven and highly motivated individuals to fill the exciting and challenging position of
General Manager EPS Factory
Reporting to the Managing Director, the General Manager EPS Factory will be responsible for providing overall leadership and oversight to the operations of the EPS Factory.
Key Duties and Responsibilities
Develop and recommend to the NHC Management and Board of Directors long term strategies, business plans, and annual operating budgets for the Factory;
Formulate the EPS strategic plan and ensure continuous achievement of set goals and objectives;
Oversee the day to day operations of the Factory and staff and ensure implementation of policies and programs;
Prepare relevant business proposals and Factory marketing plans;
Responsible for branding the Factory and its products and publicizing the EPS building technology; and
Foster a corporate culture that promotes ethical practices and good corporate governance in the Factory.
Requirements
Job Specifications
Bachelors’ degree in Engineering or Business Administration or related field from a recognised University;
Holder of a Masters degree in Finance, Strategic Management, or related field from a recognised University;
Minimum of fourteen (14) years’ work experience with five (5) years of manufacturing management;
Professional qualifications in production management or built-up environment;
Valid membership and in good standing with a relevant professional body;
Knowledge of statutory legislation governing the housing sector is desirable; and knowledge and
Demonstrate business understanding and commercial acumen.
Key Competencies
Knowledge of computerized systems relevant to the position.
A highly analytical individual with the ability to gather, analyze and evaluate facts and with the ability to prepare and present concise oral and written reports;
Demonstrate excellent managerial and leadership skills and an effective communicator;
Personal integrity with good work ethics and knowledge of principles of good corporate governance;
Ability to establish and retain effective working relationships with both internal and external stakeholders.
Candidates will be required to satisfy the following additional requirements:
Tax Compliance Certificate from the Kenya Revenue Authority;
Clearance Certificate from the Higher Education Loans Board;
Certificate of Good Conduct from the Directorate of Criminal Investigations;
Report from an Approved Credit Reference Bureau; and
Clearance from the Ethics and Anti-Corruption Commission
Benefits
Remuneration & Employment TermsRemuneration Terms
General Managers – Gross Salary: Ksh. 268,483 - 380,743 Per Month.
The positions of General Manager shall be on a three (3) year renewable contract.
