Job Description:
Job ID: JG 7 REF: KURA/RACM/REG/21/4
No of Positions: 12
Job Description
The job holder is responsible for undertaking supervision of road works; preparation of work programmes; collection of data on road inventory; preparation of tender documents and conducting annual traffic count.
Responsibilities
Undertake day to day site supervision activities for roads construction and maintenance works;
monitor Quality control activities of contracted works on site;
preparing and maintaining site records and other road work records;
Conduct surveys to collect field data on traffic, road reserve encroachments and road inventory for use in preparing roadwork and road reserve protection programmes in liaison with the supervisor;
undertake selection and location of suitable materials for Road works;
Obtain, compile and analyze all data necessary for the appraisal of road works to reconcile the available resources with the contracted scope of works;
Undertake quality control of contracted works on site;
Qualifications
Have a minimum period of four (4) years’ relevant experience in a position in the Public Service or in the Private Sector;
Have a Diploma in Civil Engineering or its equivalent qualification from a recognized institution;
Be proficient in computer applications;
Fulfil the requirements of Chapter Six of the Constitution of Kenya; and
Show merit and ability as reflected in work performance and results.
Understanding of road routine maintenance, design and maintenance supervision
Proficiency in computer applications
Data entry skills
Data analysis Skills
Interpersonal Skills
Team player
Problem solving skills

